To solve this problem, I need to track which items have been seen already and identify those that appear more than once. I'll use a set to record items we've encountered, and a list to collect duplicates in the order of their first duplicate occurrence (i.e., when they are seen for the second time). Edge cases include empty input, all-unique items (return empty list), and items that appear three or more times (only include once in the result). Also, the function should preserve the original order of first appearance for duplicates.

