I need to implement a throttle mechanism where `fn` is only executed when `tick()` has been called since the last time `fn` was invoked. The first call to `call()` should always run, regardless of whether `tick()` has been called yet. I'll use a flag to track whether `tick()` has been invoked since the last execution, and another flag to track if this is the first call. Edge cases include: multiple `call()` invocations without `tick()` in between (only the first should run), and ensuring `tick()` doesn't trigger execution by itself — it only enables the next `call()` to run.

